{
 "board": "bolt-earring",
 "note": "The bolt earring's circuit (simple_earring rev 2 with this board's 134-LED field; circuit.json) composed from blocks. Packages: the RP2350A with its flash, crystal and core regulator; the LGS4056H charger at 50 mA; the NCP730 3.3 V LDO; three TPS22913 LED-zone switches; the USBLC6 USB ESD array; the LSM6DS3TR-C IMU. Recipes for the rest: the USB-C sink; the cell's load-sharing path (a CJ2101 with its gate divided from VBUS, and a silicon diode for low leakage); the push-on power latch the MCU holds; the regulator enable, on with the latch or with USB; the edge button behind its TVS; the long press that resets the RP2350 into BOOTSEL; the battery and VBUS dividers; the light sensor; and per zone a level shifter and an LED chain. Designators are the bolt's, so the composition is the bolt part for part and net for net (crates/pinsolve/tests/bolt.rs checks it against circuit.json). Departures from the RP2350 package: no BOOTSEL or RUN buttons (long_press_reset drives both, and R2 pulls RUN up); the flash a W25Q16JV in USON-8 with CS straight on QSPI_SS (the 0 ohm link and the CS1 option omitted, its exposed pad grounded); and C8, the package's IOVDD-38 capacitor, which the bolt puts by QSPI_IOVDD (pin 54). loose.json is this board with the MCU's pins left to the solver.",
